(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[11 1 "// The interpreter's end (queue 253; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 253\"): Python/pylifecycle.c's"] [12 1 "// Py_FinalizeEx and finalize_modules (CPython 3.14.10), after the main module ran or the REPL ended. In CPython's"] [13 1 "// order: the non-daemon threads joined, the atexit functions, sys.is_finalizing() true and the other threads stopped"] [14 1 "// (a thread that takes the GIL from then on hangs, PyThread_hang_thread), sys.stdout and sys.stderr flushed (exit"] [15 1 "// status 120 when sys.stdout's flush fails), a collection (gc.collect's, its callbacks, unless gc.disable()), the import"] [16 1 "// machinery's caches cleared, then finalize_modules: builtins._ and sys's special names cleared, the standard streams"] [17 1 "// restored, every module taken out of sys.modules (CPython keeps a weak reference to each), the builtins restored to"] [18 1 "// the interpreter's first copy, a collection, the modules still alive cleared in reverse import order (their names"] [19 1 "// with one underscore first, then the others: _PyModule_ClearDict), sys's and builtins' dictionaries cleared last,"] [20 1 "// a last collection; sys.stdout and sys.stderr flushed again."] [21 1 "//"] [22 1 "// The collections at shutdown: CPython frees the dictionaries of the modules nothing holds any more as cyclic"] [23 1 "// garbage (their functions' globals and their classes make cycles), their objects' __del__ run with every global in"] [24 1 "// place. pyi's classes are held by the runtime's registries (classInfos, subclasses, the inline caches: queue 241's"] [25 1 "// finding 2), so Go's collector would keep every module that defines a class. The module dictionaries that CPython's"] [26 1 "// interpreter state no longer reaches (exitMark: sys, the builtins, the codecs' registry, what they reach through"] [27 1 "// objects, classes, functions and modules) are given to the cycle collector as dead (cyForced): the probe treats them"] [28 1 "// as garbage and an edge into one as reaching nothing, so what they alone hold is found and finalized in PEP 442's"] [29 1 "// order, while anything Go still holds by another way (a held node, a Go value) stays alive. Their dictionaries are"] [30 1 "// not cleared afterwards (CPython's tp_clear): what they hold through no node (a class's attribute, a Go container)"] [31 1 "// stays as it is, silent rather than finalized with its globals gone."] [33 1 "// sysDeletes are the names finalize_modules_delete_special sets to None in sys."] [37 1 "// siteBuiltins are the names site adds to builtins after the interpreter's copy of them (builtins_copy) is made:"] [38 1 "// the restored builtins do not have them."] [41 1 "// finalState is what the end keeps of the warnings module before it leaves sys.modules: _warnings' state (its"] [42 1 "// filters, default action and once registry), which CPython's interpreter keeps."] [49 1 "// snapshotBuiltins is interp->builtins_copy: the builtins as the interpreter starts, before site's names."] [60 1 "// Finalize is Py_FinalizeEx (Py_RunMain's end) with the program's exit status: that status, or 120 when flushing"] [61 1 "// sys.stdout failed."] [66 16 "// CPython's sys always stands: the end needs its dictionary"] [68 20 "// _Py_FinishPendingCalls: the finalizer queue's pending work"] [86 2 "// _PyImport_FiniExternal"] [103 1 "// finalizeSubinterpreters is pylifecycle.c's: subinterpreters left open warn once and are ended."] [122 1 "// flushStdFiles is flush_std_files: sys.stdout's flush (its error to the unraisable hook) and sys.stderr's, unless"] [123 1 "// closed; true when one failed."] [144 1 "// fileIsClosed is file_is_closed: f.closed true (an error: not closed)."] [154 1 "// finalizeModules is finalize_modules."] [160 2 "// finalize_modules_delete_special"] [172 2 "// finalize_remove_modules: every module out of sys.modules, in its order, then the dictionary cleared"] [194 2 "// finalize_restore_builtins"] [202 2 "// the collection: the modules nothing holds are garbage with their globals in place"] [229 2 "// finalize_modules_clear_weaklist: the modules still alive, the latest imported first"] [238 2 "// finalize_clear_sys_builtins_dict"] [241 2 "// the last collection: the dictionaries alive at the first one that nothing holds now"] [255 1 "// nativeModule is a module of the runtime's own (a C extension module's place): its dictionary is never cleared nor"] [256 1 "// given as dead (the runtime's functions may read it)."] [261 1 "// clearModuleDict is _PyModule_ClearDict: the names with one leading underscore set to None, then every name but"] [262 1 "// __builtins__, each step's dead objects finalized (reference counting's moment, at a collection). The collection is"] [263 1 "// skipped when no value the pass dropped reaches an object with finalization work due (exitReachesWork): a collection"] [264 1 "// costs Go's collector and the probe, under goi seconds."] [292 1 "// exitReachesWork is whether one of the objects reaches (exitRefs, not through a module, a module's dictionary or the"] [293 1 "// builtins) a tracked object with finalization work or weak callbacks due."] [337 14 "// a module's globals"] [349 1 "// exitCollect is _PyGC_CollectNoFail at shutdown (no gc.callbacks): the finalizer queue's rounds, the cycles with the"] [350 1 "// dead module dictionaries given (forced), the rounds again; nothing when no tracked object has work or weak"] [351 1 "// references with callbacks due. A weak reference that the interpreter state no longer reaches (mark) is garbage"] [352 1 "// itself: its callback is not called (handle_weakrefs)."] [380 1 "// exitWorkPending is whether a tracked object has finalization work, or weak references with callbacks, due."] [401 1 "// gcDumpShutdownStats is _PyGC_DumpShutdownStats: gc.garbage not empty (and no DEBUG_SAVEALL) warns ResourceWarning"] [402 1 "// \"gc: N uncollectable objects at shutdown\", the list on stderr under DEBUG_UNCOLLECTABLE."] [422 1 "// exitMarks is what CPython's interpreter state still reaches at shutdown (exitMark), by address."] [430 1 "// objAddr is o's address when o is a pointer."] [442 1 "// exitMark marks what the interpreter state holds once the modules left sys.modules: sys and its dictionary, the"] [443 1 "// builtins, the codecs' registry (its search functions, cache and error handlers), gc.callbacks and gc.garbage,"] [444 1 "// _warnings' filters and once registry, and whatever they reach through"] [445 1 "// Python's references (exitRefs: a module its dictionary, an instance its class, a class its namespace and bases, a"] [446 1 "// function its globals; a weak reference not its referent)."] [473 2 "// the collector's state: gc.callbacks and gc.garbage (gcstate's)"] [496 1 "// exitRefs calls visit with each object o references as CPython's tp_traverse sees it."] [501 11 "// a built-in type references built-in objects only"] [557 1 "// exitSkip are the runtime's structures a reference walk does not enter (a thread's frames are cleared at shutdown;"] [558 1 "// an interpreter is no object)."] [563 1 "// exitReflectRefs is the references of an object of a type exitRefs does not list (a built-in type's value: a deque,"] [564 1 "// a partial, an io object ...): the Python objects its Go fields hold, found by reflection (a closure's captures are"] [565 1 "// not seen). A failure stops the walk."] [635 1 "// finalWarnAt is _warnings.c's warn_explicit with show_warning's fallback, as the shutdown runs it once the warnings"] [636 1 "// module is gone (get_warnings_attr finds no module): the filters _warnings keeps (the warnings module's list when it"] [637 1 "// was imported, else the interpreter's defaults), the registry, then \"file:line: Category: message\" on sys.stderr, the"] [638 1 "// source line only while the import machinery stands."] [643 1 "// finalWarn is PyErr_WarnEx at shutdown: the context is the frame stacklevel up (setup_context), \"<sys>\" line 0 with"] [644 1 "// sys's registry when there is none."] [730 1 "// finalOnceRegistry is _warnings' once registry."] [741 1 "// finalAction is get_filter's answer: the first filter of _warnings' list that matches (its action), else the default"] [742 1 "// action. Without the warnings module's list, the interpreter's defaults (init_filters, no -W): DeprecationWarning"] [743 1 "// shown in __main__, ignored with PendingDeprecationWarning, ImportWarning and ResourceWarning elsewhere."] [791 1 "// finalMatched is check_matched: None matches, a plain string must be equal, else its match(arg) decides."] [808 1 "// warningsGone is whether a warning goes through finalWarn: the interpreter is finalizing and the warnings module"] [809 1 "// is not in sys.modules (get_warnings_attr imports nothing while finalizing)."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[72 54] [87 32] [114 109] [130 36] [131 35] [136 36] [137 35] [183 32] [185 28] [230 28] [230 36] [266 15] [266 25] [341 26] [412 76] [416 31] [458 32] [462 23] [542 29] [584 38] [611 14] [611 32] [621 14] [621 27] [648 32] [652 25] [655 12] [655 40] [664 37] [670 60] [683 31] [684 26] [701 26] [709 32] [722 41] [749 44] [756 29] [781 33] [782 25] [796 22]] :go/trails [[560 94]]} (go/file "pylifecycle.go" :imports [


